# Question: what do ephemeral environments, one per pull request, cost a
# month (pull requests a day × hours alive × cost per hour), and how likely
# is it to exceed 10k dollars?
#
# Run it:
#   ubc --scenario cloud/ephemeral-environments
# Change an assumption, for example environments shut down when idle:
#   ubc --set 'hours_alive = 2 to 8' --scenario cloud/ephemeral-environments
# See which assumption matters most:
#   ubc --sens monthly_cost --scenario cloud/ephemeral-environments
#
# Every "a to b" is a 90% confidence interval. Amounts are in dollars. An
# environment lives from the pull request's first push until it is merged
# or closed, nights and weekends included unless something stops it.

# Assumptions
prs_per_day = 10 to 40            # pull requests opened on a working day
hours_alive = 4 to 48             # hours an environment stays up
cost_per_hour = 0.5 to 2          # one environment: the application, a database and a preview URL
working_days = 21                 # working days in a month

# Calculation
environment_hours = prs_per_day * working_days * hours_alive     # hours of environments a month
alive = environment_hours / (30 * 24)                            # environments up at the same time on average (Little's law)
monthly_cost = environment_hours * cost_per_hour                 # the monthly bill

# Result
alive
monthly_cost
P(monthly_cost > 10k)             # how likely are the environments to cost more than 10k dollars a month?
